# Drafted reports — contain validity proofs, JWTs, secret material.
# Even in a private repo, safer to keep these on local disk only.
out/

# Logs and scratch
*.log
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.tmp
*~

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local-only credential storage — if anyone ever puts an .env here by mistake
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
secrets.yml
secrets.yaml

# Python cruft (in case any subagent helper scripts get added)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Note: memory/ IS tracked. It contains:
#   - memory/programs/*.json (per-program scope configs, useful to back up)
#   - memory/ownership-cache/*.json (verified-owned + verified-NOT-owned assets)
#   - memory/submissions/*.json (audit trail of what was drafted/submitted)
# These are mildly sensitive but contain no secret material. Private repo = OK.
#
# If you ever change to a public repo, add `memory/` to this file FIRST.
